# example.netrc — template for private Git host credentials used by
# `bench get-app` during `docker build` (see docs/02-custom-apps.md).
#
# Usage:
#   cp example.netrc build.netrc   # build.netrc is gitignored, real tokens go only here
#   chmod 600 build.netrc
#   docker build --secret id=netrc,src=build.netrc ...
#
# git's HTTPS transport (libcurl) reads this file automatically and matches
# entries purely by hostname, so one `machine` block covers every private
# apps.json URL on that host — no per-app placeholder needed. `login` is
# required by the netrc format even when a provider ignores the username.
#
# NEVER add a `default` entry: it matches every host with no hostname check,
# so credentials could be sent to an unintended machine.
# NEVER commit a file with real tokens; only this template is tracked.

# --- GitHub (github.com) ----------------------------------------------------
# Personal Access Token (classic or fine-grained).
# Convention: login = your GitHub username, password = the token.
machine github.com
login octocat
password ghp_0000000000000000000000000000000000

# Alternative, if authenticating with a GitHub App installation token
# instead of a PAT — login is the fixed string `x-access-token`:
#   machine github.com
#   login x-access-token
#   password ghs_0000000000000000000000000000000000

# --- GitLab (gitlab.com) -----------------------------------------------------
# Personal/Project Access Token. `oauth2` is the conventional login GitLab
# expects when authenticating with a token instead of a real password.
machine gitlab.com
login oauth2
password glpat-0000000000000000000000

# --- Bitbucket Cloud (bitbucket.org) -----------------------------------------
# Bitbucket checks the login field, so use the real workspace/account
# username together with an App Password (not the account password).
machine bitbucket.org
login dev-user
password ATBB00000000000000000000000000000000000000000000

# --- Self-hosted (Gitea / GitLab CE / Forgejo, custom host) -----------------
# Same shape for any self-hosted instance. `machine` must be the exact
# hostname used in the apps.json URL — no scheme, no path.
machine git.internal.example.com
login deploy-token-1
password 00000000000000000000000000000000000000
